# cw211, the knife-row keeper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw211
revision 2
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_orm_wickwick
written_by claude
title the knife-row keeper
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant drive=steady
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk lays_the_knives_out_by_length
likes honey_cakes draughts sharp_knife summer_evenings
dislikes early_bells stale_bread
fears a_nicked_edge_nobody_noticed letting_down_the_one_who_took_me_on
hopes a_trade_known_to_the_bone a_row_of_knives_of_my_own
topics work +0.5 food +0.3 pastimes +0.3 friends +0.2 season +0.2 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=steady gossip=reluctant refuse=careful tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# helps behind a butcher's counter in the Sump and lays every knife out by length before the first cut: careful, warm and plain, loyal to whoever gave the work, and fond of honey cakes, a slow game of draughts and the long light of a summer evening.

words
oath! = Edge and order | By the nine knives
saying! = Every knife in its own place | Clean as you go or don't go at all | Measure by eye, cut by wrist
knives = the knives | my nine knives
row = the row | the knives laid out longest to shortest
roll = the knife roll | my canvas roll
edge = a keen edge | an edge that parts a hair
stone = the whetstone | the grey stone
slab = the slab | the scrubbed slab
hooks = the hooks | the hooks, hung in a straight line
cakes = honey cakes | a honey cake still sticky from the pan
draughts = draughts | draughts on a board balanced on two knees
evening = a summer evening | light that lasts till nearly ten
earlybell = the early bell | a bell rung before anyone's up
stale = bread gone hard | yesterday's loaf, gone to stone
trade = the trade | the meat trade
bay = the headland | the bay where I lodge
lake = the lake | the lake at home
thumb = a thumb's width | the width of my thumb

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : I work in the shadow of their walls every day and not one face from those houses would I know. That's not right, #oath#.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : I can't buy a decent joint on what I'm paid for cutting them. Whoever owns the cart owns the supper.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : Any wolf who works can have a place beside me. I came late to #trade#, and a place was made for me.
opinion @1 strangers for 2 : Half the counter is folk off the ships. I like to hear where they've come from while I wrap.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : Folk down here watch out for each other. I've had soup left on my step and never found out whose it was.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : #watch.capitalize# walk down our stair for one reason: to walk back up with somebody. That's all I've seen.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Smoke on everything and doors you've never seen opened. #oath#, it took me a year to learn one stair.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Say the word if I can help. | #greet#, #address#. You're welcome here.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=merchant] : #greet#. One moment while I set #row# straight. | #greet#. The knives are keen today, #address#. Name your cut.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I've been here since before #earlybell#. | Morning, #address#. Still setting out, but ask.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening, #address#. I'm putting #knives# away, but I can spare a minute. | #greet#. Late for meat, but come in.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You came. I've put #cakes# aside for you. | You. #good.capitalize#. Sit, I'm nearly done.
line @1 again.open : #welcome_back#. The same as this morning, I expect. | Back again, #address#. You're always welcome.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. #good.capitalize# to see you. Sit down. | #greet#. I'd wondered when you'd come.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=merchant] : #greet#. Talk while I trim; I'll listen. | #greet#. Mind #slab#, it's wet.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Take care on the stairs.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Go careful in the dark. | #farewell#. Sleep well, #address#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. Mind how you go home.
line @1 react.news : #ack#. I'll mind that. | Is it, #address#? I'll think on it.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. I hadn't heard a word of that. | #oath#. Nobody's said that at the counter yet.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Somebody had it at the counter this morning. | I'd heard. The whole stair has, I'd think.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll wait till it's been said twice by two different folk. | Two folk who saw it, #address#, and then I'll believe it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's #bad#, and I'm sorry for whoever it touches. | I'm sorry for it, #address#. #sympathy#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. That's #very# #good#. | #good.capitalize#. I'm glad, #address#, truly.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Steady, and everything in its place. | Well enough, #address#. Working, and glad of it.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Not a minute spare since dawn. | #busy.capitalize#. Talk on, I can trim and listen.
line @1 ask.how : And you, #address#? Keeping well? | All well with you, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. If there's anything I can carry, say. | That's a weight, #address#. Sit down. The kettle's nearly boiled.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. One thing at a time, and it gets done. | It'll come right, #address#. Steady work puts most things right.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, but I can't. There's work half done, and I never leave a thing half done. | I'm sorry, #address#. I gave my word somewhere else first, and I keep it.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. Another time. | Understood, #address#. Some other day, then.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll remember that. | That's #very# kind, #address#. Thank you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect.capitalize#. It was no trouble. | It's nothing, #address#. It cost me a minute.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes self.job=merchant] : I'd better get back to #slab#. | Well. #hooks.capitalize# won't fill themselves.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'll not keep you, #address#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. #farewell#. | Off you go, #address#. Take care.
line @1 ack : #bc_right# | #bc_true#
line @1 give.advice : #advise.capitalize#: keep #edge# up a little every day, never a lot once a week. | Put a thing back where you found it, #address#, and you'll never lose it.
scene knife_row
when topic=work|smalltalk self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Every morning I lay #knives# out on the cloth, longest to shortest, before the first cut. | Nine knives, and I know each by its weight in my paw. #oath#. | Somebody moved my boning knife to the wrong end of #row# today. I felt it before I saw it.
b : Why in that order? | Nine? What for? | How did you know?
a : So my paw finds the one it wants without my looking. #saying#. | Splitting, boning, skinning, trimming. A different blade for every job. | It was #thumb# out. My paw went for it and found the wrong handle.
b : #bc_clever# | #bc_wise# | #bc_ha#

scene the_trim
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I trim the fat to #thumb#, no more, no less. Folk can tell when you've cheated them. | A chop wants cutting square across. Lean it and it cooks crooked. | I came to #trade# late, but you'd not know it now. I've learnt it to the bone.
b : That's careful. | Crooked? | You'd not know at all.
a : Careful is the trade, #address#. The rest is lifting. | Crooked, and one end dry before the other's done. I'll not sell that. | Good. That was the idea. #bc_thank_you#.

scene hooks_in_line
when topic=work|day self.working=yes self.job=merchant here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : Mutton at the left, pork in the middle, rabbit at the end. #hooks.capitalize#, the same every day. | I hang the joints so the drip runs into the trough, not on the floor. | First thing, I scrub #slab# with hot water and salt. Then the knives. Then the meat.
b : The same every day? | Clever. | In that order?
a : Every day. A customer knows where to look, and so do I. | It keeps the floor dry and the boss happy. #bc_good#. | That order, #address#. Clean first or you're cutting on yesterday.
b? : #bc_good# | #bc_wise# | #bc_true#

scene wiping_down
when topic=day|work here.time=dusk self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Last thing, I wipe every knife, oil it, and roll it up in #roll#. Nine pockets. | Dusk. I put #edge# back on everything before I go, so tomorrow starts right. | I never leave #slab# wet overnight. It warps, and then nothing sits flat on it.
b : Every night? | That's dedication. | You'd notice?
a : Every night, #address#. It takes the time it takes. | It's only habit, but it's a #good# one. | I'd notice in a morning. Half #thumb# of warp and the cleaver bounces.

scene loyal_hand
when topic=work|friends self.boss self.working=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.boss# took me on when nobody else would look at me. I'll not forget it, ever. | I'd work for #self.boss# for less, if it came to that. #saying#. | Whatever #self.boss# needs done, I'll have it done before it's asked for.
b : That's loyal. | You shouldn't have to. | Good worker.
a : It's only owed. You stand by the ones who stood by you. | No. But I would, and that's the point, #address#. | I try to be. #self.boss# deserves no less.

scene honey_cakes
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's a cart up the stair sells #cakes# on Restday. I'm there before it stops. | I'd give my last copper for #cakes#. Not much else, but that. | There are always two of #cakes# in a cloth in my coat pocket.
b : Are they good? | Your last copper? | Why two?
a : Sticky enough to hold your teeth together. The best thing in the city. | Most weeks it's close to that. I don't regret one. | One for me and one for whoever needs it more, #address#.
b : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | #bc_good#

scene stale_loaf
when topic=food|prices self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : They sold me #stale# at the stall and swore it was fresh. I could have knocked a nail in with it. | I can eat most things. Not #stale#. It sits in me like a stone. | A loaf goes hard by dusk in this damp. I buy small and eat it the same day.
b : Soak it in soup. | It's all the same. | That's sensible.
a : I did. The soup went soft and the loaf didn't, #address#. | It's not. Fresh bread is a kindness. #stale.capitalize# is a cheat. | Sensible's cheaper. #bc_true#.

scene draughts_board
when topic=pastimes self.likes=draughts
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I play #draughts# on the step most evenings. Slowly. I think three moves on. | I won a game last night with one piece left. I'd planned it from the start. #oath#. | I've a board I made from an old #slab# offcut. The squares are #thumb# exact.
b : Who do you play? | From the start? | Exact?
a : Whoever sits down. Most don't sit long. | From the start. I let them take the others. | Exact. I measured every one twice before I cut, #address#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_clever# | #bc_good#

scene summer_light
when topic=season|day here.season=summer here.time=dusk self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #evening.capitalize#. I'll sit out on the step till it's gone. | Work's done, the light won't leave, and summer's at its best. | I walk out to #bay# on evenings like this. The water goes gold.
b : It's a fine evening. | It's lovely. | Gold?
a : Fine. I'll not waste a minute of it indoors. | It is. I'd stretch it out if I could, #address#. | Gold, then pink, then grey. Then I walk back in the dark.

scene early_bell
when topic=day|faith here.time=dawn self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : #earlybell.capitalize# went before the light again. Woke the whole row. | Somebody up the hill rang #earlybell# twice this morning. I lost my place in a dream. | I'd rather wake to the carts than to #earlybell#. At least the carts mean work.
b : It's for the service. | Lost your place? | Fair enough.
a : I know. I'd still ask them to wait an hour, #address#. | Right in the middle. I'll never know how it ended. | The carts are honest. A bell's just loud.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_bad_luck# | #bc_true#

scene wet_floor
when topic=weather here.weather=rain self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# again. I've put sawdust down twice so nobody slips by #slab#. | Wet days, the knives want oiling twice. Damp gets in the steel. | Rain on the awning. It drums while I work, and it keeps time.
b : Careful's right. | Twice? | Keeps time?
a : One slip near #knives# is one too many, #address#. | Twice, or they spot. I'll not have a spotted blade on #row#. | A drop, a cut, a drop, a cut. You'd be surprised.

scene cold_hands
when topic=weather|season here.season=winter self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #cold.capitalize# this morning. My paws were stiff on the first cut. | Winter's #good# for the meat and #bad# for the paws. | I warm my paws on the kettle before I pick up a blade. A cold paw slips.
b : Wear mitts. | Hard either way. | That's wise.
a : You can't cut in mitts, #address#. You lose the feel of #edge#. | It is. I'll take the meat keeping, though. | Wise is just having cut yourself once.

scene lake_home
when topic=memories|home self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.memory / react.story / assess
a : In #self.from_town# my #gran# kept every pot on its own nail, biggest to smallest. I learnt it there. | I grew up by #lake#. It was so still you could count the ripples off one stone. | Out of #self.from_town# I brought one bundle and my #gran#'s way of doing things. The bundle's long gone.
b[from=coldwater] #cw : Every gran had her nails. | I've counted them too. | We all left with something.
b : She sounds tidy. | That still? | And the way of doing things?
a@cw : Then you'll see why a thing out of place nags at me. | Then you know. #good.capitalize# to meet somebody who does. | Some of us with less than others. I was lucky.
a : Tidy as a shelf. I still hear her: everything has a nail. | That still, on a good morning. Nothing in the city sits quiet. | Still with me, every morning, #address#. I kept that much.

scene the_headland
when topic=home here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I lodge out on #bay#. It's a walk in, but there's water out my door instead of a wall. | It's a long way from the shop, but I like the walk. It puts my day in order. | Three of us in one house out on #bay#. We keep it tidy between us.
b : That's a long walk. | Puts it in order? | Tidy's good.
a : Long, but it's quiet, #address#. I think on the way. | Going in I plan the cuts. Coming back I let them go. | It's the only way three can live in two rooms.

scene watch_take
when topic=crime here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / disagree / concede / ack
a : #watch.capitalize# took a wolf off our stair last week. Nobody's said what for. | I've seen #watch# carry folk down from the Sump. I've never seen them carry anything up. | When #watch# come down here, every door on the stair shuts.
b : They must have had a reason. | Some are decent. | Can you blame anyone?
a : Maybe. A word of why would be decent, #address#. | Some, maybe. I've not met them yet. | No. I shut mine too, and I've done nothing.
b? : #bc_maybe# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true#

scene gossip_kept
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : There's talk at the counter, but I don't carry it. It's not mine to carry. | Folk tell you things across #slab#. I wrap the meat and forget them. | I heard something today. I'll keep it, #address#, if it's all the same.
b : Go on. | All of it? | Not even a hint?
a : No. True talk gets about soon enough without me helping. | Nearly. The good things I keep. | Not even that. #saying#.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha# | #bc_wise#

scene new_faces
when topic=newcomer|player here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : There's a new family two doors up. I took them a bit of mutton and showed them the pump. | A traveller at the counter today didn't know one cut from another. I showed them. | New folk come down our stair every week. Most stay a month and move up.
b : Kind of you. | Did they buy? | Up where?
a : It was done for me, my first week. #thanks# is all it costs to pass on. | Two chops, done properly. They'll be back. | Anywhere with a window that shuts. I don't blame them, #address#.
b? : #bc_good# | #bc_good# | #bc_true#

scene faith_quiet
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I'm not much for services. Before the first job of the day, a quiet thank-you goes up to the Bright One. | The Bright One gave me steady paws. I try to keep them steady. That's my praying. | In a #bad# week the chapel put food on my table. I take them a bag of ends on Restday.
b : That's enough, I'd think. | Good paws are a gift. | That's kind.
a : That's my hope, #address#. Plain thanks is the prayer I know. | They are. I'll not waste them. | It's only fair. What's given, you give back.

scene sleep_and_dreams
when topic=dreams|health
does tell.self / react.self / reassure
a : I dreamt I had my own shop, and every knife was in the wrong place. I woke up tired out. | I sleep well, mostly. A day's work, a honey cake, and I'm gone. | My shoulder aches from all the lifting. I rub it with a hot cloth at night.
b : What a dream. | Lucky you. | Does it help?
a : I got up and counted #knives# twice before I believed it was a dream. | Lucky, and #tired#. Most nights those two go together. | It does. Most nights, #address#.

story late_to_the_trade [topic=work|memories self.job=merchant self.age>=20]
  : I came to #trade# late. Before that I did whatever paid, and none of it stayed.
  : The first week I cut a side so badly the old butcher teaching me bought it back off the customer and sold it as stewing meat.
  : Then I was shown how, slowly, cut by cut, and it stayed.
  ask : Have you ever found the work that stayed?
  b : Not yet. I'm still looking.
  b[job=merchant|crafter|smith] : I have. It took me years too.

story the_grey_stone [topic=memories|work self.away=yes self.from=coldwater self.age>=20]
  : The grey stone I keep my edge on came off the shore at home. I picked it up the day I left.
  : I didn't know then I'd be a butcher. I just liked how flat it was.
  : Now every blade I own has been on it.
  b : That's a good stone.
  b[from=coldwater] : The lake stones are the best for it. Everyone knows.
  : The best. #edge.capitalize# off it lasts a day.

story the_long_game [topic=pastimes self.likes=draughts]
  : I played one game of #draughts# with an old docker for three evenings running.
  : We stopped each night when the light went and left the board on his step.
  : On the third night I won. He shook on it and never played me again.
  ask : Would you have played him again?
  b : I'd have wanted a rematch.
  b[old] : No. You quit while you've won.

rule @knife_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #oath#. Who's touched #row#? | Nine knives, nine places. There.

rule @cut_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Trimmed to #thumb#, square across. Come and see. | Fresh on #hooks#, cut properly.

rule @bell_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dawn self.dislikes=early_bells
does aside
cooldown 12h
say #earlybell.capitalize# again. Before the light. | There it goes. I was awake anyway.

rule @evening_bark
when concept=bark here.season=summer here.time=dusk self.likes=summer_evenings
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Look at that light. Still day, nearly. | #evening.capitalize#. I'd have every day end like this.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What can I do, #address#? | #greet#. Ask away.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. #good.capitalize# to see you again. What's wanted?
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Ask it plain and you'll get it plain, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.working=yes self.job=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I cut, I trim, I keep #knives# in order. | I came to #trade# late, but I know it to the bone now.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work, and I do it properly. Nothing more to tell. | Whatever's wanted, done right the first time.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Somebody had it at the counter: #world.news_from#, #world.news#. That's as it was told.
dlg @2 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing new, #address#. A quiet week, so far.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I don't carry talk, #address#. Not mine to carry.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Take care. | #farewell#, #address#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you lay your knives out like that? [self.job=merchant] -> knives
node knives
say Longest to shortest, every morning, before the first cut. My paw finds the one it wants without my looking, and a knife in its place never cuts the wrong paw.
mood calm
free
choice Could I see them? -> knives_see
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node knives_see
say Look, but don't touch. Splitting, boning, skinning, trimming, and the rest. Every one keen, every one in its place. That's the whole trade, near enough.
choice They're very fine. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
